  "equipment_type": "Sensor (particulate matter)",
  "applies_to": "DFRobot SEN0662 Gravity BMV080 module with its DIP switch set to UART, firmware V1.0.0 / register map version 4, per the DFRobot wiki register page.",
  "summary": "The SEN0662 is a maker-grade particulate sensor board built on the Bosch BMV080. With its DIP switch on the UART side it acts as a Modbus RTU slave. Input registers give PM1.0, PM2.5 and PM10 as big-endian floats plus status; holding registers set the address, serial format and measurement mode and start or stop measurement.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 87,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Registers are listed as hex protocol addresses from 0x0000 and sent unchanged; the wiki's example reads PM1.0 with start address 0x0006 on function 04."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "V1.0.0 (0x1000), register map version 0x0004",
  "source": {
    "title": "Gravity: BMV080 PM2.5 Air Quality Sensor - Modbus Register Definitions (SEN0662 wiki)",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://wiki.dfrobot.com/sen0662/docs/25056",
    "pages": "Register table at the top; function and exception codes; read example (57 04 00 06 00 06)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the wiki says registers are big-endian and the high word comes first, and its example response 40 E0 00 00 decodes to 7.0 ug/m3, so floats are ABCD.",
    "The default slave address is 0x57 (decimal 87). The board's I2C address pins do not affect it.",
    "The sensor does not measure after power-up: write 1 to holding register 0x0003 after every power cycle before reading PM values.",
    "The Integration Time float has no unit printed in the table; it is listed without a unit.",
    "The wiki also documents a broadcast read of holding register 0x0000 (address scan) that only works with a single device on the bus; it is a vendor extension, not standard Modbus."
  ],
